{
  "description": "Case sensitivity of G, M and C strkeys. StrKeys are uppercase RFC 4648 base32. A strict decoder MUST reject any lowercase character with INVALID_BASE32 unless the caller opts in with allowLowercase, in which case the input is normalized to uppercase, reported with normalized: true, and then subject to every other check (length, base32, checksum). Only ASCII a-z count as lowercase: case folding MUST be ASCII-only, so non-ASCII letters that uppercase to A-Z (e.g. U+017F) are INVALID_BASE32. Check order: prefix (UNKNOWN_PREFIX), lowercase (INVALID_BASE32), alphabet (INVALID_BASE32), length (INVALID_LENGTH), trailing bits (INVALID_BASE32), checksum (INVALID_CHECKSUM).",
